/*
 * Declares the VoidType class.
 *
 * A void value is a value with no data. It's not compatible with a empty tuple
 * value as void cannot be used to describe a variable or a value content, only
 * to describe that functions won't return a value.
 *
 * Void value carries a mutability information as they are addressable, and used
 * in pointers to describe a pointer that points to something that is not
 * defined, but can be mutable.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::native::scalar::void_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/native/scalar/void_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
